#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#CarSim allows you to build and simulate vehicles with Rack and Pinion or Recirculating Ball steering systems. Both of those can be manual or power-assisted.
#
#In this example, an open-loop steering torque apply-and-release maneuver is performed with an E-Class sedan equiped with a manual Rack and Pinion steering system. It is overlaid with a simulation of a nearly identical vehicle, the only difference being the other vehicle has a power-assisted Rack and Pinion steering system.
#
#Use the plots and animation to analyze the results of these tests to understand the differences the steering system type has on a vehicle's response.
